{
  "about": "Records that name their own key (SPEC 3.6.1). H(tag, a, b, ...) is SHA-256 over the tag in UTF-8 right-padded with zero bytes to 32, then each 32-byte piece. identity = H(\"veilcore:v1:commit\", recordSecret); keySalt = H(\"veilcore:v1:keysalt\", recordSecret); keyBinding = H(\"veilcore:v1:keybind\", identity, keySalt); contentHash = SHA-256 of the canonical serialisation of fields (keyBinding included), or, when fields carry a field set (fieldSchema and fieldSetRoot, SPEC 4.5), H(\"veilcore:v1:frecord\", fieldSetRoot, that SHA-256); fingerprint = H(\"veilcore:v1:keyrecord\", keyBinding, contentHash), or contentHash when fields has no keyBinding. A check matches when the fingerprint recomputed from identity, keySalt and contentHash equals the fingerprint; inputs are 64 lowercase hex characters, anything else does not match. A record whose keyBinding is present but not 64 lowercase hex is refused, and so is one with only one of fieldSchema and fieldSetRoot, or either not 64 lowercase hex.",
  "source": "contract/scripts/key-bound-vectors.mjs (node:crypto and veilcore-records canonicalise); regenerate, never edit by hand",
